back", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01N9MkzChCA7eMoxHCLwBB2Y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01AaDUXtvE4y9ARnTxb4nt5N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, and eu-west). Per the runbook, I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions. The rollback reported VERIFIED with all three regions on v2.3.0. v2.3.1 remains flagged unhealthy and should not be redeployed until the failure is root-caused. Follow-up: confirm error rate has recovered and investigate the v2.3.1 regression.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy and running in every region.\n- **Current state:** The service reports healthy on v2.3.0, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the v2.3.1 failure and the rollback. It notes that v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until the root cause is found.\n\nNo change-manager approval was needed, since v2.3.0 has already been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}